#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:1
msgid "Hercules DJ Console 4-Mx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:3
msgid ""
"The Hercules DJ Console 4-Mx is a USB controller with a built in sound card."
" It is very similar to the {ref}`Hercules DJ Console RMX "
"<hercules_dj_console_rmx>`, but with switches for 4 decks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:5
msgid ""
"[Manufacturer's product "
"page](https://support.hercules.com/en/product/djconsole4mx-en/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:10
msgid "Audio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:12
msgid ""
"The DJ Console 4-Mx is not a USB class compliant MIDI device, although it is"
" a USB Audio device. Drivers for Mac OS X and Windows can be found on the "
"[Hercules support "
"page](http://ts.hercules.com/eng/index.php?pg=view_files&gid=17&fid=62&pid=263&cid=1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:16
msgid ""
"The controller will not work on Linux out of the box. You will need to use "
"the [Linux usermode driver](https://github.com/mixxxdj/mixxx/wiki/Hercules-"
"Linux-Usermode-Driver). The device will only produce audio if the device "
"hasn't been configured for ASIO under windows previously. Also, check the "
"volumes in alsamixer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:20
msgid ""
"The sound card has 4 inputs and 4 outputs (2 stereo in/out). The inputs are "
"switchable between line-in and phono, and also is possible to select "
"different line levels (consumer -10dBV, Pro +4dBu and boost +8dBu ), so you "
"can connect both CD players and turntables on the inputs. \\* Inputs are "
"RCA. \\* Outputs are RCA or 1/4\" TRS balanced. \\* Microphone input is "
"1/4\" TS \\* Headphone jack is 1/4\" (6.35 mm) TRS stereo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:24
msgid "Hercules Tray Icon configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:26
msgid ""
"The drivers for Windows and OS X install an application that can be used to "
"configure the audio and controller settings. Most of the settings work well "
"on the default setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:28
msgid ""
"**Volume/Pan/Mute**: Sets the volume output for channels 1-2 and channels "
"3-4. Note that the volume of the channels 3-4 refers to the line output from"
" behind. In other words. It does not affect the volume of the headphones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:30
msgid ""
"**Line in mode**: Sets the line level of the inputs. In case of line 1-2, it"
" also allows to redirect the microphone to the line 1-2. Else, it is mixed "
"in hardware to the main out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:31
msgid ""
"**Talkover attenuation**: Sets how much to attenuate the main output when "
"activating the hardware mixed microphone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:32
msgid ""
"**Enable/Disable jog wheels**: Allows to disable the jog wheels, in case the"
" user desires not to use them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:33
msgid ""
"**Sensitivity**: Alters the sensitivity of the jog wheels. If you change "
"this, change also the sensitivity option in the script, as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:34
msgid ""
"**Audio Mode**: Enables the WDM drivers (non-asio) or the specific ASIO-only"
" driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:35
msgid ""
"**MIDI pitch resolution**: Sets the resolution of the pitch sliders. Mixxx "
"will work with any of the two settings, but it is recommended to set it to "
"14bit (8bit used) which doubles the precision versus 7bit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:37
msgid ""
"**ASIO**: You can configure the samplerate, bit depth and latency for the "
"ASIO driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:38
msgid ""
"**MIDI channel for controls**: *Keep these at 1-2 (Default) when you use it "
"with Mixxx.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:39
msgid ""
"**Crossfader settings**: Allows to configure how does the crossfader react. "
"Mixxx also offers an alternate invert option in the crossfader settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:40
msgid ""
"**Headphone channels**: Allows to setup which input channels are sent to the"
" headphone output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:41
msgid ""
"**Channels 1-2 hardware mix**: Allows mixing the line in or the microphone "
"directly in hardware to the speaker output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:42
msgid ""
"**Deck mode**: *Leave this at 4 Decks (Default) if you want to use four "
"decks with Mixxx. Else, you will only be able to use two decks.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:44
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:46
msgid ""
"There are several options that can be configured for this mapping. You can "
"edit these by opening the JavaScript file in a text editor like Notepad, "
"TextEdit, or gEdit and editing the values at the top of the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:49
msgid ""
"**autoHeadMix**: Indicates if the headphone/main mix should automatically be"
" set to main when none of the headphone cue buttons are activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:50
msgid ""
"**autoHeadcueOnLoad**: Automatically enable the headphone cue select (PFL) "
"of the deck when a song is loaded. (Like in virtual-dj)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:51
msgid "**beatFlashLed**: set which LED, if any, blinks with the beat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:52
msgid ""
"**useVuMeters**: Simulate vuMeters using the kill and source buttons’ LEDs. "
"If enabled, shows main VUs, or deck VU depending if prefader listen button "
"is enabled or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:53
msgid ""
"**naviScrollSpeed**: KeyRepeat speed for navigating up/down, in "
"milliseconds. 100 is a good value. Lower values make it scroll faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:54
msgid ""
"**crossfaderScratchCurve**: The controller has two modes to report the "
"crossfader position. The default/beatmix curve, and the scratch curve. The "
"default curve reports the real position of the control. The scratch curve "
"just crossfades on the edges. Setting this setting to true, the curve will "
"change to scratch curve when the scratch mode is on (scratch button). "
"Setting it to false will not change it, so it will use the setting "
"configured in the DJHercules Tray-icon configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:57
msgid ""
"**vinylSpeed**: Playback speed of the virtual vinyl that is being scratched."
" 45.00 and 33.33 are the common speeds. (Lower number equals faster scratch)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:58
msgid ""
"**sensitivity**: Jog wheel sensitivity. You should configure this setting to"
" the same value than in the DJHercules tray icon configuration. (Normal "
"means 1/1). If crossfaderScratchCurve is true, or the setting is changed "
"while Mixxx is active, this value will be detected automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:60
msgid ""
"**alpha**: alpha value for the scratch filter (start with 1/8 (0.125) and "
"tune from there)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:61
msgid ""
"**beta**: beta value for the scratch filter (start with alpha/32 and tune "
"from there)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_dj_console_4_mx.md:62
msgid ""
"**FXbuttonsSetup**: This indicates which mapping for the FX buttons should "
"Mixxx use. The possible values are: mixxx21, mixxx20, and original (Hercules"
" Manual and the default setup in Virtual DJ 7 LE)"
msgstr ""

